{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5617) that requires implementing srd106-df requirements R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3 for the `cmd/df` utility. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all filesystems are reported successfully\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any error occurs (inaccessible FILE argument, invalid option), printing diagnostics to stderr\n   - R4.3: Must install SIGPIPE handler at startup via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   \n   The task requires modifying `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go`, adding differential test cases, and verifying all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against `gdf` (GNU df from Homebrew)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 for success, 1 for errors\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for test output parity\n   - Normalizer functions for program name differences (`gdf:` vs `df:`)\n   - The cobbler orchestrator manages git; no git commands allowed\n   - Must follow execution constitution (E1-E10) and go_style_constitution\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd106-df.yaml`** - SRD defining all df requirements. R4 section (lines 110-118) defines exit codes and signal handling:\n     - R4.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R4.2: Exit 1 on error with stderr diagnostic\n     - R4.3: SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   \n   - **`cmd/df/main.go`** (632 lines) - Existing implementation covering R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.7. Key observations:\n     - Line 62: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` already called (R4.3 already implemented)